504 0 obj
<< /A << /O /Layout /Placement /Block >> /Alt (Flowchart depicting the structure of fisheries management. The process begins at the National Fisheries Office for policy formulation and enforcement, moving through the Fisheries Department to Country Fisheries Offices, with Coastguard involvement. National BMU Network connects to Indian Ocean Water Body management, followed by County BMU Networks and Landing Site BMUs. The final stage involves an Executive Office, Sub-committee, and Assembly Members. Management and development focus on collaboration between national officers and provincial levels, with sub-community numbers varying between four and seven.) /K 535 0 R /P 229 0 R /Pg 218 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
endobj
505 0 obj
<< /A << /O /Layout /Placement /Block >> /Alt (A flowchart depicting a fishery data workflow diagram, including the stages of Preparation, Implementation, Data Handling, and Assessment & Integration. The Preparation stage involves data collection and stakeholder identification. Implementation covers stakeholder meetings, data collection by fishers and traders, and literacy evaluations. Data Handling includes data extraction, coding, cleaning, and analysis. Assessment & Integration involves social-ecological assessments, stakeholder forums, and public awareness efforts. Key metrics include fishing efforts, catch-per-unit efforts, and individual income, integrated into community and neighborhood information.) /K 536 0 R /P 229 0 R /Pg 219 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
endobj
506 0 obj
<< /A << /O /Layout /Placement /Block >> /Alt (Map of Kenya's coast showing study sites with a legend for landmarks including towns and protected areas. Sites are marked with treatments from one to five, each with different dashboard access levels for fisheries information. Colors in the legend correlate to the map, indicating different data access treatments ranging from no feedback to detailed community and individual data. An inset map shows the location of the area within Kenya.) /K 537 0 R /P 229 0 R /Pg 221 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
endobj
